    "name": "E•••••• J.",
    "service": "Website rebuild",
    "text": "The business had good demand, but the website kept getting in the way. The client had a business website that had been moved between hosts and agencies so many times no one knew what was canonical. The audit uncovered redirect chains, duplicate staging URLs, mixed analytics, old sitemaps, and conflicting metadata. Instead of adding another patch, we documented the domain history, consolidated redirects, cleaned canonicals, and rebuilt the deployment process. The team was included in the reasoning rather than receiving another black-box handoff. In the end, future changes stopped creating new search and tracking problems. The project changed the conversation from “what broke this week?” to “what should we improve next?”",
