    "name": "F•••••• Q.",
    "service": "SEO architecture",
    "text": "The project began with a problem that looked smaller than it was. The client had a service website that had been patched by three different developers over almost two years. The audit uncovered navigation bugs, duplicated scripts, and a quote form that failed intermittently on mobile. Instead of adding another patch, we mapped the old code, rebuilt the shared components, and migrated the content without changing the URLs customers already used. We worked through the problem in stages so the business could keep operating while the risky pieces were replaced. In the end, the owner finally had one stable system instead of another temporary fix. The team could see exactly why each page and interaction existed.",
