    "id": 118,
    "name": "H•••••• I.",
    "service": "Local growth",
    "text": "The site had been “almost finished” for months, but every new fix exposed another weak point. The client had a company that had changed services several times without changing the website architecture. The audit uncovered old offers still dominating navigation, new services buried in dropdowns, and sales staff sending prospects to different pages. Instead of adding another patch, we remapped the information architecture around current revenue, created clear service destinations, and retired obsolete paths with redirects. In the end, the website began describing the business that exists now instead of the company from five years ago. The strongest feedback was that people stopped asking where to click and started asking about the service itself.",
