    "text": "We came in after the team had already tried several fixes. The client had a professional practice with a homepage that looked polished but produced very few qualified inquiries. The audit uncovered generic messaging, weak proof, multiple equal-weight calls to action, and no clear explanation of who the service was for. Instead of adding another patch, we rebuilt the hierarchy around the actual decision clients make, moved proof closer to the offer, and simplified the contact path. We tested edge cases with long content, small screens, slow connections, and failed form submissions instead of only checking the happy path. In the end, the team stopped blaming traffic and could see where the website had been creating friction. The site became easier to improve because the team finally understood the architecture underneath it.",
