    "text": "We were contacted after another round of changes failed to hold. The client had a service website that had been patched by three different developers over almost two years. The audit uncovered navigation bugs, duplicated scripts, and a quote form that failed intermittently on mobile. Instead of adding another patch, we mapped the old code, rebuilt the shared components, and migrated the content without changing the URLs customers already used. We tested edge cases with long content, small screens, slow connections, and failed form submissions instead of only checking the happy path. In the end, the owner finally had one stable system instead of another temporary fix. The final site was cleaner, but the real win was the reduction in uncertainty behind it.",
