    "service": "SEO architecture",
    "text": "The project began with a problem that looked smaller than it was. The client had a law firm site that had accumulated years of articles without a coherent content architecture. The audit uncovered duplicate topics, old legal references, orphan pages, and several URLs competing for the same search intent. Instead of adding another patch, we audited the library, consolidated overlapping pages, created practice-area hubs, and established a research workflow with sources and update dates. In the end, the content library became easier for both attorneys and search engines to navigate. The final site was cleaner, but the real win was the reduction in uncertainty behind it.",
