    "service": "Security recovery",
    "text": "The site was not completely broken, which made the underlying problem easy to ignore. The client had a B2B company whose lead form worked but sent inquiries into a shared inbox nobody owned. The audit uncovered slow follow-up, missing context, duplicate responses, and no reliable connection between marketing source and sales outcome. Instead of adding another patch, we redesigned the form, added sensible qualification, routed leads into a clear workflow, and preserved campaign context. The hardest part was separating symptoms from causes because previous work had layered new code, plugins, redirects, and content on top of decisions nobody had documented. By the end, the internal team knew where leads went, who owned each system, and which metrics should trigger the next improvement. In the end, the website became part of the sales operation rather than a message box. The launch felt less dramatic than the months before it, which was exactly the point: the system finally behaved predictably.",
