    "text": "The team did not need another theme; they needed the system untangled. The client had a restaurant group with several sites and inconsistent menus, hours, and reservation links. The audit uncovered duplicate content, outdated location information, broken structured data, and mobile users landing on desktop-style menus. Instead of adding another patch, we standardized location data, rebuilt the responsive templates, cleaned the structured data, and made reservations the obvious next step. We simplified the number of moving parts before we added any new feature, which made every later improvement easier to reason about. In the end, the digital experience stopped contradicting what guests saw in the real locations. The launch felt less dramatic than the months before it, which was exactly the point: the system finally behaved predictably.",
